# Master-Thesis — Code summary (root README)

This repository collects code used in the Master thesis: ANSYS projects, DMS discrete optimizer, MATLAB postprocessing, verification data and an RL optimization scaffold.

Top-level folders
- Code Ansys
  - ANSYS APDL scripts and input/output text templates used by the FEM evaluations.
- Code Ansys Reference
  - Reference inputs and example outputs for regression/verification.
- Code Results
  - MATLAB scripts to postprocess ANSYS outputs, compute EMCC, select optimal patch placements and produce plots.
- Code Verification ANSYS
  - Exported verification datasets (control vs no-control) used for validation.
- DMS_Discreto.6_multivariavel
  - Discrete Multi-Start (DMS) driver and ANSYS interface (driver_dms_discreto.m, funcFF.m, logs, pareto files).
- GLODS_Discreto_RL_1.0
  - RL / discrete global optimization scaffold (placeholder). See GLODS README for details.

Quick usage / workflow
1. Configure ANSYS path and permissions so MATLAB can launch ANSYS batch runs (see DMS_Discreto.6_multivariavel/funcFF.m).
2. Run optimizer:
   - DMS (example): open MATLAB, add repository to path, run:
     >> cd('DMS_Discreto.6_multivariavel')
     >> driver_dms_discreto
   - RL (planned): implement env wrapper and training script in GLODS_Discreto_RL_1.0.
3. After evaluations, run postprocessing:
   - Open Code Results and run:
     >> result_optimal_position_multiobj_modal
     >> result_harmonic_analysis
4. Visualize / verify using files under Code Verification ANSYS.

Notes & recommendations
- Use a cache or surrogate when experimenting to avoid repeated costly ANSYS runs.
- Maintain consistent working directory when scripts call or write files (many scripts expect relative paths).